      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Zn(OAc)2·2H2O (0.2 mmol, 0.0439 g), Yb(OAc)3·4H2O (0.2 mmol, 0.0844 g) and H2L1 (0.2 mmol, 0.0937 g) were dissolved in 5 mL CH3OH, 5 mL EtOH and 2 mL DMF at room temperature, then NEt3 in EtOH (0.35 mol L−1, 1 mL) was added. The mixture was stirred and heated under reflux for 30 min, cooled and filtered. Diethyl ether was allowed to diffuse slowly into the filtrate at room temperature, giving pale yellow crystals after one day. Crystals were filtered, washed with EtOH (3 × 5 mL) and dried under air for one day. Reactions were performed under dry oxygen-free dinitrogen using Schlenk techniques.",
